UNIVMAR — Feature Specification
Stone Company Management Platform

FEATURE: Sales, Quotation, Inventory & Order Management

1. FEATURE OBJECTIVE

This feature manages the complete commercial flow of a stone company, from the first customer request to the final delivery.

Main business flow:

Customer / Company
→ Project
→ Request for Quotation (RFQ)
→ Quotation
→ Customer Acceptance
→ Order
→ Stock Reservation
→ Preparation
→ Delivery
→ Invoice / Payment

The objective is to make UNIVMAR behave like a real stone-company management system rather than a simple e-commerce website.


2. MAIN ACTORS

Administrator
- Manages users, roles, permissions and system configuration.
- Has visibility over all business operations.

Sales Agent
- Manages customers and companies.
- Receives quotation requests.
- Creates and sends quotations.
- Converts accepted quotations into orders.
- Follows customer projects and negotiations.

Inventory Manager
- Manages stone inventory.
- Records stock entries, adjustments and movements.
- Manages slab, lot or bundle availability.
- Confirms stock reservations and releases.

Purchasing Manager
- Manages suppliers.
- Creates purchase orders.
- Tracks incoming stone, slabs, bundles and materials.

Customer
- Browses available stones.
- Creates quotation requests.
- Follows quotations and orders.
- Accepts or rejects quotations.
- Accesses commercial documents.

Manager
- Monitors sales, stock, margins, quotations, orders and performance.


